[{:seon.task/name "a-stalled-eval-ends-with-its-error", :seon.task/plan "Found by context, 2026-11-13 (notes: evidence/context-refine-hang-2026-11-13.md): a refine's turn-9 eval ran grep -rl over its checkout and blocked in open(2) for 80 minutes; the agent proc recorded it :stalled {:quiet-ms .. :last-op {:kind :tests}}, and nothing ended the eval or answered it with an error, so the run waited until a person ended the grep. Nothing may hang (docs/errors.md#nothing-crashes-and-nothing-hangs): a stalled eval is ended, its child processes with it, and answered with a typed error naming what it waited on, so the turn goes on and the agent reads why. Owner: runtime (the stall in seon.agent-proc, its answer in seon.system's back-op). Proof: an eval whose child blocks forever (a read of a FIFO no one writes) is answered with that error, and the agent's next eval runs.", :seon.task/kind :work, :seon.task/proofs #{seon.agent-test/a-stalled-eval-is-answered-with-its-error}}]
